//! Charter `H-CLAIMS` models, generated by `proptest_scheduler_claim_models`.
//!
//! The property drives the real public startup validator
//! (`slicer_scheduler::validation::validate_startup_dag`) against independent
//! models derived from the reviewed exception table in
//! `docs/spec_packets/proptest-openrscad_07_pbt-scheduler/packet.spec.md`
//! §"Charter H-CLAIMS" and `docs/01_system_architecture.md` §"Claim System":
//!
//! * claim scopes are typed tuples `(object_id, region_id, Option<layer>)`,
//!   never concatenated strings, so two distinct tuples can never alias;
//! * global ordinary/raft holders conflict pairwise, duplicate observations of
//!   one module do not, and the four `FILL_CLAIM_IDS` plus the four finite
//!   family-support globals are exact exceptions;
//! * the four stable claims keep one holder per object across every region and
//!   layer, while `claim:sparse-fill` / `support-generator` transitions stay
//!   permitted;
//! * write ordering is decided by exact shared paths, `ir_reads` consumption of
//!   that same field and a real `StageDag` path, plus the bounded
//!   `SupportPlanIR`/`SupportIR` family-support roots;
//! * module/capability membership, direct/transitive stage legality and an
//!   enabled-only effective universe are modelled from `STAGE_ORDER` rank;
//! * the startup selection/pairing seams
//!   (`dedup_same_claim_modules_with_typed_wall_generator`,
//!   `resolve_held_claims` and `validate_support_family_pairing`) are driven
//!   through a declarative selector table, so the generative half is not only
//!   the deterministic control.
//!
//! The models never call the private validator passes: they recompute the
//! expected diagnostics from the request the case builds. `tests/
//! property_scheduler_contracts.rs` mounts this module for the deterministic
//! controls, so every helper here is a plain target-private test module, not a
//! new SDK API.

#![allow(dead_code)]

